# The SQLite era, and the benches that still write there. `prospections.db` is a
# REAL ledger — businesses, a signed deal, an amount actually collected. Real
# client data in a public repository is the mistake that already cost this
# project its entire history; a commit does not remove it, only a new history
# does. It stays out, and it stays out by rule rather than by vigilance.
